            "text": "So pressing 'W' opens the prompt \"What do you want to wear? [g or ?*]\" but the autohalt dismisses the menu and it says \"Never mind.\" The prompt is waiting for input, but the system auto-dismisses it.\n\nThe problem is that after pressing 'W', the game shows a prompt waiting for item selection, but the MCP system's autohalt kicks in and auto-dismisses the menu before I can press 'g'.\n\nLet me try calling np_wear with item_letter=\"g\" but without the prior prompt being open. Actually, let me look at this more carefully. When I call `np_wear(item_letter=\"g\")`, it logs \"Skill 'wear g' completed\" with \"Invalid direction for 'g' prefix.\" This suggests it's sending the 'W' command and 'g' separately, and 'g' is being interpreted as a regular command rather than a menu response.\n\nActually, maybe the issue is that the autohalt dismisses the wear prompt before 'g' can be selected. Let me try the `np_wear` function with no arguments at all, but this time the prompt should auto-dismiss.\n\nActually, I think the real issue is that the MCP server might need the item letter as a specific argument. Let me look at the server source code.\n\nLet me search for the nethack skill files to understand how arguments are passed.",
